Z||000004||California Kid||09-01-2001||12:37 AM||||Roger,  Thanks for posting on the show above, but think I'll pass to.  Do you know any details on the Springfield 2001 show taking place Sept 7-9th @ the Clark Co. Fairgrounds in Springfield?? Just curious as to what kind of show it is.  Also listed is the NEOCC Fall Classic in Kent, Ohio (same dates).<P>For the Drag Race guys near Michigan, on Sept. 8th Royal Pontiac Drag Series, Milan Dragway, Milan Mich. 248-855-6291.<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"> The season is starting to wind down, really disappointed because I skipped alot of nice shows during the hot spell we had.||||reg||1
Z||000005||rogergarrison||09-01-2001||07:38 AM||||they have them 2 times a year. The 'Show' is just to show your car, no competetion or awards. Its a huge swap meet with used parts and new parts vendors. also a car corral where they sell lots of cars, some great buys. I saw a 88 Porsche 944 last year, only needed a cracked dash replaced and a little touch up paint sell for $2500. Its ez to find right off the side of I-70.||||reg||1
